{"name":"Hawk Feather","hex":"#ae8c5c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hawk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A diurnal predatory bird of the family Accipitridae, smaller than an eagle.","Any diurnal predatory terrestrial bird of similar size and appearance to the accipitrid hawks, such as a falcon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt with a hawk.","To make an attack while on the wing; to soar and strike like a hawk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hawk"},{"term":"feather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds, used for flight, swimming, protection and display.","Long hair on the lower legs of a dog or horse, especially a draft horse, notably the Clydesdale breed. Narrowly only the rear hair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or furnish with feathers;  to fletch.","To adorn, as if with feathers; to fringe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hawk","blocks":[{"text":"Hawks are birds of prey of the family Accipitridae. They are very widely distributed and are found on all continents, except Antarctica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Northern_Goshawk_ad_M2.jpg/330px-Northern_Goshawk_ad_M2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawk","wikidata":"Q846664"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1